    ThreadedHasher: an offline index counts nothing and toasts nothing
    
    #308 1-raoffline claude F-RA-05. With the hash library absent (offline),
    the constructor has ProxyCards say the new games wait for the link and
    empties its queue -- but mTotal had been taken from the queue first and
    kept the waiting games' count. So `mTotal == 0` did not return: an index
    card and threads were made for an empty queue, the destructor toasted
    INDEXING COMPLETED. UPDATE GAMELISTS TO APPLY CHANGES. beside the card
    saying nothing was indexed (two surfaces, one false), and the threads,
    ending at once, could delete the hasher before start() read mTotal and
    set mInstance from it. mTotal is set to 0 with the queue.
    
    Test: tests/hasher-offline-index.py compiles the shipped constructor and
    destructor out of ThreadedHasher.cpp against a stand-in class with the
    same members and runs an offline index with three games waiting. Before:
      FAIL an offline run counts nothing to index
      FAIL no index card and no threads over an empty queue
      FAIL no INDEXING COMPLETED toast beside the offline card -- got:
      INDEXING COMPLETED. UPDATE GAMELISTS TO APPLY CHANGES.
    After: hasher-offline-index: PASS (five checks). es-syntax-check PASS.
    
    Already written: nothing inherited -- a run's counters.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/es-app/src/ThreadedHasher.cpp b/es-app/src/ThreadedHasher.cpp
index 648a24e6f..b2547d475 100644
--- a/es-app/src/ThreadedHasher.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/ThreadedHasher.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,14 @@ ThreadedHasher::ThreadedHasher(Window* window, HasherType type, std::queue<FileD
 					ProxyCards::indexRanOffline(mWindow, (int) mSearchQueue.size());
 				while (!mSearchQueue.empty())
 					mSearchQueue.pop();
+				// And nothing is counted: mTotal was taken from the queue
+				// above, so it stayed at the games that were waiting. A card
+				// and threads were made for an empty queue, the destructor
+				// toasted INDEXING COMPLETED beside the offline card, and the
+				// threads -- ending at once -- could delete this before
+				// start() read it back (#308 1-raoffline claude F-RA-05).
+				// With 0, the check below returns before any of that.
+				mTotal = 0;
 			}
 			else
 				sCheevosLibraryCame = true;
